Message catalog maintenance
===========================

Each po/meson.build registers a catalog in nls_catalogs.  Sources normally
come from the corresponding compilation lists.  Shared sources must be
assigned to the domains that use their messages; linking a static library
does not imply that every message in that library belongs in every client.
Include conditional sources in extraction even when they are not compiled.

The common targets are defined after all catalogs have been registered.
init-po and <catalog>-init-po generate <catalog>.pot in the build tree's
src/tools/nls directory.  update-po and <catalog>-update-po generate
<catalog>-<language>.po.new there, using same-language catalogs as compendia.
The source PO files are never overwritten.  Languages are taken from the
registered catalogs' LINGUAS files; add a new translation there so Meson
reconfigures the language and dependency lists.

The nls.py helper stages extraction inputs under stable source-root-relative
names, rewrites generated #line references, and converts the resulting
references to catalog-directory-relative names.  This avoids build-root
paths in catalogs without rewriting message text.  Generated files with no
source counterpart retain their logical build-tree-relative names.

Register grammar .y files explicitly alongside the compilation sources.
When both a .y file and its generated .c file are present, extraction uses
the grammar, excluding Bison skeleton messages.  Scanner .l files are build
dependencies, but extraction uses their generated C: parsing Flex regular
expressions as C can lose messages.  Other generated inputs, such as
sql_help.c and guc_tables.inc.c, must be passed as Meson targets.  Included
C fragments and headers with messages also need explicit registration.

The targets are incremental and are not part of the default build.
xgettext and msgmerge are optional native maintainer tools.  Compilation
and installation of existing translations continue to use i18n.gettext()
and only apply to enabled components.

The nls/catalogs Meson test exercises extraction and merging with gettext,
including generated references, plural flags, compendia, and failed merges.
When changing source selection, compare message IDs, plurals, contexts,
format flags, and translator comments against the previous catalogs.  Also
compare catalogs from minimal and feature-rich configurations and check
that a second init-po or update-po invocation does no work.
